msgid "Overview of of application research tools for solving differential equations."
msgstr "Ikhtisar alat riset aplikasi untuk menyelesaikan persamaan diferensial."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial differential equations"
msgstr "Persamaan diferensial parsial"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial differential equations {#partial-differential-equations}"
msgstr "Persamaan diferensial parsial {#partial-differential-equations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This active area of research explores how quantum algorithms can help solve partial differential equations that describe physical systems and processes, such as fluid dynamics, heat transfer, electromagnetic fields, and quantum mechanical systems. Approaches include quantum algorithms for linear systems of equations, which can be applied to certain discretized differential equations, as well as quantum methods for differential equations that directly exploit quantum circuits or quantum state representations. These techniques can offer computational advantages for specific large-scale problems, particularly when the solution can be efficiently encoded in and extracted from a quantum state. However, their practical benefits depend on factors such as problem structure, data encoding, hardware requirements, and the cost of retrieving the solution.\n"
msgstr "Bidang riset yang aktif ini mengeksplorasi bagaimana algoritma kuantum bisa membantu menyelesaikan persamaan diferensial parsial yang menggambarkan sistem dan proses fisik, seperti dinamika fluida, perpindahan panas, medan elektromagnetik, dan sistem mekanika kuantum. Pendekatannya mencakup algoritma kuantum untuk sistem persamaan linear, yang bisa diterapkan pada persamaan diferensial terdiskretisasi tertentu, serta metode kuantum untuk persamaan diferensial yang langsung memanfaatkan Circuit kuantum atau representasi state kuantum. Teknik-teknik ini bisa menawarkan keunggulan komputasi untuk masalah berskala besar tertentu, terutama ketika solusinya bisa dienkode secara efisien ke dalam state kuantum dan diekstrak darinya. Namun, manfaat praktisnya bergantung pada faktor seperti struktur masalah, pengodean data, kebutuhan hardware, dan biaya pengambilan solusi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common workflow encodes a trial solution as a parameterized quantum circuit, then classically optimizes the circuit parameters so that the resulting quantum state approximates the true solution of the differential equation across a set of sample points. This variational approach can accommodate boundary and initial conditions, and can be combined with multiple classical optimizers in sequence to improve convergence. The application function on this page automates this workflow for specific domains, so that you can supply physical parameters and boundary conditions directly, without implementing the underlying encoding and optimization loop yourself.\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja yang umum mengenkode solusi percobaan sebagai Circuit kuantum berparameter, lalu mengoptimalkan parameter Circuit secara klasik sehingga state kuantum yang dihasilkan mendekati solusi sebenarnya dari persamaan diferensial di sekumpulan titik sampel. Pendekatan variasional ini bisa mengakomodasi kondisi batas dan kondisi awal, dan bisa dikombinasikan dengan beberapa optimizer klasik secara berurutan untuk meningkatkan konvergensi. Application function di halaman ini mengotomatiskan alur kerja tersebut untuk domain tertentu, sehingga kamu bisa langsung memberikan parameter fisik dan kondisi batas, tanpa harus mengimplementasikan sendiri loop pengodean dan optimasinya.\n"

